1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,552
Everybody can build now.

2
00:00:02,902 --> 00:00:05,360
An app. A website.

3
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:07,173
A whole business idea.

4
00:00:07,273 --> 00:00:09,730
Stuff that used to take a whole team?

5
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:12,166
One person and a prompt.

6
00:00:12,266 --> 00:00:14,812
And that’s wild, when you really sit with it.

7
00:00:15,312 --> 00:00:17,912
But here’s the part nobody wants to talk about.

8
00:00:18,062 --> 00:00:20,405
If everybody can build…

9
00:00:20,405 --> 00:00:23,560
building ain’t the advantage anymore.

10
00:00:23,810 --> 00:00:27,227
Nobody cares how fast you made it

11
00:00:27,227 --> 00:00:28,975
if it doesn’t solve a problem.

12
00:00:29,375 --> 00:00:32,912
So the question isn’t, “what can you create?”

13
00:00:32,962 --> 00:00:36,481
It’s, “what can you make work?”

14
00:00:36,731 --> 00:00:39,110
Something people need.

15
00:00:39,110 --> 00:00:41,792
Something they actually use.

16
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:43,582
Something worth paying for.

17
00:00:44,032 --> 00:00:47,195
AI changed who gets to build.

18
00:00:47,195 --> 00:00:49,905
It didn’t change why people buy.

19
00:00:50,455 --> 00:00:51,727
Quiet Bands.

20
00:00:51,427 --> 00:00:53,285
Build what matters.

